    "body": "pulse task #2906 \u00b7 generation 1.\n\n<!-- pulse-operation:f331407b7807056566e4d7fb996d8939 -->\n\nassigned to @PORTALSURFER. the frozen task plan is retained in pulse and copied below.\n\n# Pulse task #2906: Sampler MVP: save and reopen sample state, media and tuning\n\nOperation: f331407b7807056566e4d7fb996d8939\nAssignee: PORTALSURFER (Pulse #1, GitHub ID 41680373)\n\nTarget: save a current-format project containing the Sampler, close/reopen it through the real project flow, and recover the same sample sound/settings/tuning. Acceptance: exact media/content references, supported pitch/gain/bounds/loop/envelope and project tuning survive; relative/existing path policy is preserved; missing/changed media produces truthful recovery/refusal without destructive replacement. Cover actual project save/open and underlying storage/history fixtures, including failed/cancelled open preserving the current project. No backwards compatibility or legacy migration requirement during alpha; no database/media reset.\n\nOwner: existing integration/Native storage flow, Local UI only where required; no new writer. Depends on sample loading; independent current-format roundtrip tests are ready now. Clear with retained identities/settings/tuning plus matching rendered/played result after reopen, not a serialized field-only assertion.\n\nSplit from #2789/canonical PR395, goal5 Playable Sampler MVP. Existing implementation/source/history stays intact. Intake draft is planning linkage only until deliberate focused source handoff; no automatic task start, duplicate implementation or replacing existing canonicalPR395. Do not mark complete from parent merge/component tests without this target's evidence.\n\ncreated by pulse shared PR intake/start task. builds, checks and merging follow the repository's own instructions.",
